== Strategy ==
Ideally, multiple players should work together to efficiently defeat the boss. Since the player has a higher chance of receiving rare drops if they deal more damage than other players, many players attempt to maximize their DPS.

Bows are the best way to deal damage against the main boss, as well as being the safest. One of the most cost-effective setups to kill the '''Magma Boss''' consistently is using at least 2 pieces of {{Item|Terror Armor}} and a {{Item|Juju Shortbow}} as Hydra Strikes can damage the boss very effectively. The late game bow, the {{Item|Terminator}} does an even better job and can consistently deal maximum damage per Normal phase to reach the max damage threshold. This allows a solo player to defeat the boss at the fastest time indistinguishable from cooperative play due to the aforementioned mandatory three jumps from the boss per cycle.

Note that {{LI|Arrow}}s can often bounce off the Magma Boss due to [[mcw:Damage#Immunity|Minecraft mechanics]].

Magic weapons can be used to deal damage during the Normal phase, but are not as effective as shortbows even if using a {{Item|Hyperion}} with powerful armor. It is highly effective in clearing out mobs during the split and fleeing phase though.

Using a melee weapon is a much riskier strategy of damaging the boss, due to it being commonly guarded by the AOE attacks, and is harder to hit. Melee builds are also nearly useless during the Split phase as the magma cubes especially the Unstable Magma will certainly kill the player. It is not advised to undertake this strategy unless they have very effective armor such as {{Item|Necron's Armor}} or {{Item|Crimson Armor}}. If the player has a good bow, melee is not recommended outright.

When the boss splits into smaller cubes, players should go after the Glares, since they are the ones responsible for the massive multiplicative damage. If using the {{Item|Hyperion}}, try using Wither Impact above them instead of directly towards them to reduce the chances of teleporting into them.

When entering its Fleeing phase, it will always first start moving diagonally towards negative-X and negative-Z (towards the [[Hellwisp]] area). Use the time when it's reforming to camp the spot as mage or to aim towards it as an archer to immediately kill it.

When the boss dies, each player gets separate drops. If a player quits the lobby, gets limboed, or exits the game when the items are dropped, they will not receive the items.

== Trivia ==
*The '''Magma Boss''' was the first boss added and revamped from an early-game boss to a late-game boss.
*The {{Item|Ember Rod}} used to be a drop from the '''Magma Boss''' but was later removed.
**{{Item|Ember Fragment}}s also used to drop from the '''Magma Boss''', but have since been replaced with {{Item|Rekindled Ember Fragment}}s.
*Contrary to popular belief, the player is not required to land the killing blow to have the '''Magma Boss''' count towards their [[Bestiary]].
* While an {{Item|Aurora Staff}} does not work on the main boss, it does on {{MobSprite|Magma Glare;Magma Glares}} and {{MobSprite|Unstable Magma;Unstable Magmas}}.
* The '''Magma Boss''' is not affected by [[Derpy|Derpy's]] double HP perk during its normal and fleeing states. 
**The {{MobSprite|Magma Glare;Magma Glares}} and {{MobSprite|Unstable Magma;Unstable Magmas}}, however, are.

== Bugs ==
*The '''Magma Boss''' occasionally gets stuck during the flee state, becoming immobile and invulnerable.
**This can possibly happen if the chunks are unloaded during the final split state.
**This can be fixed by pushing it into the lava so it goes through blocks to take suffocation damage.
**No loot will appear on its death if it stays in this bugged state for too long.
